  "worked_solution": "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)=4x-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=2$ and $x=4.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)=4x-{x}^{2}$ between the lower limit $x=2$ and the upper limit $x=4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{2}^{4}4x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$",
